[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Liner notes is installed but NOT enabled or started.
New installation guide (DOCS): %%DOCSDIR%%/INSTALL.md

Daemon: %%PREFIX%%/sbin/liner-notes
Administration: %%PREFIX%%/bin/liner-notes-admin
Configuration: %%ETCDIR%%
Editable menus/help/banner: %%DATADIR%%
Logs: /var/log/liner-notes
Supervisor PID: /var/run/liner-notes.pid
Data and private transfer spool: /var/db/liner-notes
Service: liner_notes (default: 127.0.0.1:2222)
Management commands: liner-notes-admin (maintenance alias retained), liner-notes-vaultctl,
liner-notes-memberctl. Python and SQLite are required.

Review %%ETCDIR%%/liner_notes.conf, then use:
  sysrc liner_notes_enable=YES
  service liner_notes start

Keep the listener private while creating the first BBS account and setting
liner_notes_admins. Reuse an existing instance only after an offline backup.

ZMODEM is optional. Use the official FreeBSD comms/lrzsz port for resume support.
The spool must be owned by liner_notes and mode 0700. Enable the helper in
liner_notes.conf after preparing the engine. Before using resume, run
liner-notes-check-resume as the service user and save its --receipt to
/var/db/liner-notes/lrz-resume.json. Regenerate it after replacing lrz. External SSH uses the system's
OpenSSH; liner-notes-ssh does not configure sshd or system login accounts.

Updates: %%DOCSDIR%%/UPGRADING.md (DOCS option).
The resume checker can be rerun without deleting its existing receipt.
Source releases: https://github.com/matsuotakeshi/liner-notes/releases
License: GPL-3.0-only; bundled xterm.js retains MIT notices.
Official UID/GID allocation is still required before Ports Collection submission.

With WEBUI enabled, read WEBUI.md before enabling liner_notes_web. Configure
web/web.toml for your HTTPS origin and actual BBS port. Existing templates and
messages are preserved. Neither service is automatically started.
When replacing a preview runtime, set liner_notes_program to the installed
/usr/local/sbin/liner-notes only after verifying that executable exists.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  message: <<EOM
Installation paths changed in 0.65_1. Stop and back up before upgrading.
Edited settings/assets and old /var/db/liner_notes data are not moved.
Review liner_notes.conf.sample and PORTS.md before restarting. Update the
program/home, menus/help/banner, helper, data, logs and PID paths in your
existing configuration and rc.conf. The rc script rejects a known old home
or unselected old default data instead of starting a new empty BBS.
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
BBS data and edited configuration are preserved. The liner_notes account is
also retained. Do not delete these until backups and migration are verified.
EOM
}
]
